{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1484651-i-want-to-share-my-next-chronicle-and-look-for-some-opinions-advice","id":1484651,"title":"I want to share my next Chronicle and look for some opinions/advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-21T14:42:11-07:00","id":1484651,"title":"I want to share my next Chronicle and look for some opinions/advice","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> This is something I was thinking of doing or not, but finally I really see people here are very nice and very creative, and maybe I can be the former but I don't feel the later.<br /> <br /> In a week I start a new Chronicle on the spanish twitch channel of my partner, and I really want to create an interesting story that last five to ten chapters but with the possibility of last more. I feel excited but anxious at the same time, so I want to share some of my thoughs here.<br /> <br /> The game is a Hunter: The Vigil 2e Chronicle. Tier 1 on scale but one of the player is technically Tier 2, for more on them I leave a spoiler on the players.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> <b>Player 1, Aiden Carter: </b>A Telequinetic student of medicine, with a very defensive Vigil. A lot of their themes are about the protection of the child of the girl they couldn't saved and some egoist thoughs about &quot;I don't care if there exist monster eating the flesh of the innocent, but don't dare to eat the flesh of <i>my</i> innocents&quot;. He also has contact with a pretty good Mage that only wants stability on the town so she can still working on her Mistery.<br /> <br /> <b>Player 2, Alyss Warren:</b> A Medium that finish High School and live with their family. The family have a lineage of female mediums that all vow to the same Vigil: Mantain the balance between the dead and the living, the supernatural and the normal, this the one that I consider Tier 2 for how we create and structure the family as a Compact. Is a pretty innocent girl with interest on giving the supernatural to the general public and break the Veil, incapable of believing on the monstruos nature of &quot;bad supernaturals&quot;. Vampire drink blood because they are hungry, ghost haunts because they are in pain. Is impossible to this beings to be evil without a reason, no? I'm excited for this one because the player says to me she wants the character to be broken.<br /> <br /> <b>Player 3, Andrew Witney:</b> A private investigator, after a encounter with a cultist a strange mark on their hand give them the Mind of a Madman and Postcognition capabilities, the mark is strange on nature and he does anything for mantain it hidden. He knows the supernatural is evil and corrupt people, he saw how their tutor was corrupted killing innocents and guilties alike. He promise to never kill a human, no matter how evil they are.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The players knows this part of the premise: They all live on Humanity Street on a fictional Ireland (I do my best to research, but I don't feel confident to say &quot;this happen on Ireland&quot;), the middle class district of the big city is one of peace and tranquility. Except that, three weeks ago, a old lady knows as Alana dissapear from their house without a trace. Police is searching, but no so much, more distress by the year long dissapearance of a big industrial fish than a nobody old woman probably missing on the streets. The characters care for this lady, two of them for the community, the last for work. In the background, a new technology company is open business Dimini Labs, working to make a name of Fake-Dublin as a place of technological progress.<br /> <br /> The characters also know two clues: The first is one is something they need to think if they will share or not: The Slabhra\u00ed Fuilithe gang seems to be connected with the missing persons, but the connection is thin, some witness hear the vehicle, another saw a guy that fit the description of one of the leaders, and most important, all of this witness are related to the second clue, a clue they can't share with the police: Ghost are missing, every day less ghost walk the Twillight and strange creatures the Mage describe as &quot;Claimeds&quot; appear more and more. All of the people that knows about the gang, is people involved on the supernatural, ghosts, mediums and spirits. <br /> <br /> The play will start with them going to the place of the gang, unfolding the mistery from there.<br /> <br /> <b>What is really happening?</b><br /> <br /> What the players don't know is: I read a lot of Deviant and I really like the premise of Conspiracies from the Deviant point of view, players know what are Conspiracies from Hunter pov but not as this institutions of pain.<br /> <br /> Dimini Labs is a Standing 3 Conspiracy, and they work hard to get to that place. The Conspiracy wants to developt new products that use ghostly essence as a source of esoteric technology. The Avernus System is they most succesfull product: A mechanical implant on the nervous system that let them borrow knowledge of a dozen of ghost trapped inside the implant. (In mechanical effects, they can have the benefits from Amalgam Form with 3 dots without being a Deviant or loss individual personality). This is not without a price, employees of various forms were test subjects of horrible experiments, only one of this employees survived, a Coactive Devoted that was tasked with the &quot;securing&quot; of more test subjects, using his new ghostly powers this Devote work hard as the leader of the Slabhra\u00ed Fuilithe. They also have some minor Invasive Devoteds they create on the pursue of new technologies.<br /> <br /> The Conspiracy kidnap Alana for the creation of a Avernus <i>Dynamic</i> System, capable not only of capitalize on the knowledge of the ghost even better than before (having the six points of Amalgam) but forcefull summon this beings from the other world. The head of research wants to create a being capable to <i>enter</i> on the other world to further their resource pool for new Avernus Systems, drive mad by the idea of science being the ultimate weapon to control into submission the supernatural: The Head of Research is a Hunter, but a pretty deranged one. The executive chief, on exchange, is only interested on the money, some of their products are very popular between the rich, but the personality of the Research Team is leaving the executive board without followers, only employees capable of betraying at any moment.<br /> <br /> The idea is the characters find that Dimini Labs is involved on the kidnaps and what they are using that kidnaped people, all the players (except the Medium on first glance) have reasons to collaborate or fight against the conspiracy, and the Conspiracy is low standing and with internal trife that make easy to destroy their nodes.<br /> <br /> This is all I have for now, I don't want to write a lot because I know no campaign plan survive first contact with the players, but the general idea is there.<br /> <br /> Any advice, opinion, or even a simple support word is welcome.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T22:21:34-07:00","id":1484758,"title":"","content":"Sounds pretty interesting so far, I think following the logistics can provide a lot of ways to flesh out <i>Dimini</i>'s train of thought: Anchors need to be transported, how are they doing so and how are they storing them ? How are they preventing ghosts from Manifesting, attacking or otherwise breaching containment ? Anchors react to the ghost being remembered, are they experimenting using brainwashing and drug treatment to increase the amount of Essence harnessed ? Ghosts have two coins for moving through the Underworld, are they making deals in exchange for groups scouting the Underworld for the impending invasion ? How much data are they collecting ? Have they started gaining key allies in River Cities, so that they can setup a logistical pipeline to support their campaign of conquest ?<br /> <br /> An idea that comes to mind is that its very difficult to make the first headway into developing ghost affecting tech without &quot;delving into occult mumbo-jumbo that undermines the safety, consistency and scalability that only the scientific method can provide&quot;, so perhaps an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1319624-101-exarch-cults?p=1329818#post1329818\">Exarchal cult</a> I wrote some time ago could be helpful. Its a Mystery Cult merit that is 3 antagonists in one, with the greater cult creating 3 sub-organizations in an assembly line, processing humans to create bleeding edge technology. They would probably be interested in <i>Dimini Lab's</i> research, making the entire Underworld into a commodity is very resonant with the Chancellor's ethos. Plus, if they get a cut of especially interesting test subjects, then they could probably furnish the knowhow and provide agents to support on the field. This way they have an easy gateway to know more about the God-Machine and ghosts (from the Seers watching over it), plus each of them have agents and facilities that could add one more disturbing element to complement the theme of profiteering science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-23-2022, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}